public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public Person(String name, int age) {
        this.name = name;
        this.age = age;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (o == null || getClass() != o.getClass()) return false;
        Person person = (Person) o;
        return age == person.age && Objects.equals(name, person.name);
    }
}
```

This `equals` method checks whether two objects are equal based on their `name` and `age`. If the `age` is the same and the `name` is also the same, then the objects are considered equal.
